// The pressure Poisson solve, laplacian(p) = div(u).
//
// Weighted stencil rather than a flat divide by six. A face's contribution and
// its share of the divisor go together:
//   open side or top - Dirichlet p = 0 outside, so the ghost adds nothing to the
//                      sum but still counts in the divisor;
//   solid floor      - Neumann dp/dn = 0, so the ghost equals p(c) itself. Moved
//                      to the left-hand side that removes one from the divisor,
//                      which is the correct no-flux condition. The old code
//                      instead copied the row above into row 0, which imposes
//                      the condition on the wrong side of the face and leaks.
//
// The solver never clears the pressure field, warm-starting each frame from the
// previous solution — the plume is quasi-steady, so it starts close.
//
// Dense: one Jacobi sweep per dispatch, the reference discretisation.
//
// Sparse: the 10^3 halo cache is loaded once and then relaxed several times in
// place before anything is written back, so a dispatch is a block solve rather
// than a sweep (block-Jacobi / additive Schwarz — the halo is frozen for the
// duration, which is still a valid smoother because the block diagonal of a
// weakly diagonally dominant M-matrix is one). Two things come out of that:
// global passes and barriers drop by the inner sweep count, and the in-place
// update makes the interior Gauss-Seidel rather than Jacobi. Red-black ordering
// keeps that deterministic — a cell's six neighbours are all of the other colour,
// so no thread reads a value another thread is writing — and over-relaxation
// (omega > 1) then costs nothing on top.
//
// Information still only crosses a tile boundary once per dispatch, but it now
// crosses the tile itself within one, so the sweep is no longer limited to one
// cell of propagation per global pass. The long wavelengths that neither ordering
// reaches are what fire_press_coarse is for.

void main() {
	ivec3 c = cell_coord();
	if (out_of_grid(c)) {
		return;
	}

	ivec3 gmax = grid_max();
	float sum = 0.0;
	float divisor = 5.0; // the five faces that are always open or interior

	sum += (c.x < gmax.x) ? load_press_src(c + ivec3(1, 0, 0)) : 0.0;
	sum += (c.x > 0) ? load_press_src(c - ivec3(1, 0, 0)) : 0.0;
	sum += (c.y < gmax.y) ? load_press_src(c + ivec3(0, 1, 0)) : 0.0;
	sum += (c.z < gmax.z) ? load_press_src(c + ivec3(0, 0, 1)) : 0.0;
	sum += (c.z > 0) ? load_press_src(c - ivec3(0, 0, 1)) : 0.0;

	// Downward face: interior below row 0, solid at it.
	if (c.y > 0) {
		sum += load_press_src(c - ivec3(0, 1, 0));
		divisor += 1.0;
	}

	float h = params.cell.x;
	store_press_dst(c, (sum - h * h * load_diverg(c)) / divisor);
}
